          "text": "WAN Ssŭ-pei 萬斯備 (T. 允誠, H. 又庵), poet and calligrapher, was a native of Yin-hsien, Chekiang. He was the seventh son of Wan T'ai [q. v.], son-in-law of Li Yeh-ssŭ (T. 李鄴嗣, H. 杲堂, original ming 文胤), and a pupil of (T. Huang Tsung-hsi).",
